/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 65 0 R
/T (Flask. The system uses applicant information such as income, co-applicant income, loan amount, loan term, credit score, existing loans, savings, education, employment status, marital status, dependents and property area. Categorical values are converted into numerical representations using One-Hot Encoding, while missing values are handled using imputation. A Random Forest Classifier with 200 estimators and a maximum depth of 10 is trained on the prepared dataset. The web dashboard accepts a new applicant profile and displays the predicted loan decision together with approval/rejection probabilities and a simple risk category.)
/E (Flask. The system uses applicant information such as income, co-applicant income, loan amount, loan term, credit score, existing loans, savings, education, employment status, marital status, dependents and property area. Categorical values are converted into numerical representations using One-Hot Encoding, while missing values are handled using imputation. A Random Forest Classifier with 200 estimators and a maximum depth of 10 is trained on the prepared dataset. The web dashboard accepts a new applicant profile and displays the predicted loan decision together with approval/rejection probabilities and a simple risk category.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [27]
>>
